From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:10:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/smmstore: Optionally keep the MRC cache on a vboot
 slot switch

SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_TRY_OTHER, the setup's "Go back to" the other RW
slot, erases RW_MRC_CACHE first, so that the other slot trains the
memory itself. On the M920x that costs a 21-36 s training on the next
boot, and it is not needed there: the cache carries a version, the
FSP-M image revision of the slot that wrote it with the board's bits
(Hyper-Threading and a hash of the processor, through
FSP_PLATFORM_MEMORY_SETTINGS_VERSIONS), and its data hashes. Each slot
has its own FSP-M, so a slot that cannot use the cache sees another
version and trains, and one that can skips the training.

SMMSTORE_VBOOT_SWITCH_KEEPS_MRC_CACHE makes vboot_try_other() keep the
cache. It is defined outside "if SMMSTORE", and the m720q_m920q boards
select it only with SMMSTORE, so that a build without SMMSTORE has no
unmet dependency (fatal with KCONFIG_WERROR). Without it, as on the
W541, the cache is erased as before. Update the comment of the command
in smmstore.h.

A release that changes the memory settings on the coreboot side
without a new FSP-M or version bits would now reuse the other slot's
cache after a switch; with the cache erased it trained. Clearing the
cache (update.py other-slot --retrain, or erasing RW_MRC_CACHE) is the
way out then.

TEST=Host syntax check of smi.c and store.c for SMM with the option on
and off. For the hardware test, between two builds with patch 0173
(the first boot after ci-151 retrains once, the cache version changes
from 7007420 to 7007430): "Go back to" in the setup, then on the other
slot "MRC: 'RW_MRC_CACHE' does not need update" and no training, and
the same back; a slot with another FSP-M trains once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/drivers/smmstore/Kconfig             | 12 ++++++++++++
 src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c               |  8 +++++---
 src/include/smmstore.h                   |  4 +++-
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/Kconfig |  1 +
 4 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/drivers/smmstore/Kconfig b/src/drivers/smmstore/Kconfig
index b5d9a90fd8..d47493b3ea 100644
--- a/src/drivers/smmstore/Kconfig
+++ b/src/drivers/smmstore/Kconfig
@@ -30,3 +30,15 @@ config SMMSTORE_BLOCK_SIZE
 	  an internal SoC or board policy value, not a user-visible option.
 
 endif
+
+# Outside "if SMMSTORE": a board selects it whatever its payload
+config SMMSTORE_VBOOT_SWITCH_KEEPS_MRC_CACHE
+	bool
+	help
+	  SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_TRY_OTHER, the payload's switch to the other
+	  vboot RW slot, keeps the memory training cache (RW_MRC_CACHE)
+	  instead of erasing it. Select it only where the version of the
+	  cache tells each slot whether it can use it: the FSP-M of the
+	  slot, and the board's memory settings with
+	  FSP_PLATFORM_MEMORY_SETTINGS_VERSIONS. A slot that cannot use it
+	  trains the memory itself, one that can skips the training.
diff --git a/src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c b/src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c
index 29e2cfe05b..5c902fc55a 100644
--- a/src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c
+++ b/src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@ static int range_check(void *start, size_t size)
 /* SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_TRY_OTHER refused until the next boot */
 static bool vboot_locked;
 
-/* The memory training cache, if the FMAP has one, which another slot must not reuse */
+/* Erase the memory training cache, if the FMAP has one, so that another slot trains again */
 static int erase_mrc_cache(void)
 {
 	struct region_device rdev;
@@ -260,9 +260,11 @@ static uint32_t vboot_try_other(void)
 		return SMMSTORE_RET_FAILURE;
 	/*
 	 * The cache first: if the switch does not happen after that, the slot
-	 * of now only trains the memory again.
+	 * of now only trains the memory again. Kept where its version decides
+	 * whether the other slot can use it.
 	 */
-	if (erase_mrc_cache() || vbnv_try_other_slot(2))
+	if ((!CONFIG(SMMSTORE_VBOOT_SWITCH_KEEPS_MRC_CACHE) && erase_mrc_cache()) ||
+	    vbnv_try_other_slot(2))
 		return SMMSTORE_RET_FAILURE;
 	return SMMSTORE_RET_SUCCESS;
 }
diff --git a/src/include/smmstore.h b/src/include/smmstore.h
index 01f7c82d12..1eea78171c 100644
--- a/src/include/smmstore.h
+++ b/src/include/smmstore.h
@@ -29,7 +29,9 @@
  * its payload sends SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_SLOT_GOOD; if it does not verify or
  * does not get that far, vboot goes back to the slot that runs now. The
  * memory training cache (RW_MRC_CACHE), if the FMAP has one, is erased first,
- * as an update capsule does, so that the other slot trains the memory itself.
+ * as an update capsule does, so that the other slot trains the memory itself;
+ * with SMMSTORE_VBOOT_SWITCH_KEEPS_MRC_CACHE it is kept, and its version
+ * tells the other slot whether it can use it.
  *
  * The rules of the setup that asks for it apply here too, so that code that
  * runs before the payload locks the switch (a Driver#### or SysPrep####
diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/Kconfig b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/Kconfig
index c75234511a..4713cb6cee 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/Kconfig
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/Kconfig
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@ config BOARD_SPECIFIC_OPTIONS
 	select MAINBOARD_HAS_TPM2
 	select MAINBOARD_USES_IFD_GBE_REGION
 	select MEMORY_MAPPED_TPM
+	select SMMSTORE_VBOOT_SWITCH_KEEPS_MRC_CACHE if SMMSTORE
 	select SOC_INTEL_CANNONLAKE_PCH_H
 	select SOC_INTEL_COFFEELAKE
 	select SOC_INTEL_COMMON_BLOCK_HDA_VERB
